    "poster_id": 621197,
    "post_rendered": "Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\"  width=\"11\" height=\"8\" > be a  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\"  width=\"10\" height=\"8\" > -th primitive root of unity. Given complex numbers <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/0/2105defb85241467940294a12eaa07c49c9044fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1,a_2,\\cdots,a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"103\" height=\"11\" >,</span> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"11\" > of them are non-zero. Let<br>\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/c/2dc637e9f3591edd96f07ce55013adbcd5815c7a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"$$b_k=\\sum_{i=1}^n a_i \\omega^{ki}$$\"  width=\"107\" height=\"47\" >for <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/7/687148e576426186af9168da61f09c5b000e2bf7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=1,2,\\cdots, n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"114\" height=\"16\" >.</span> Prove that if <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/2/6823f9e12a69e16d2e0871f7178e88efd968a477.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" >,</span> then at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/5/7e519cd1bc9443b459bee2e062682a17bba6e66f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{n}{p}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -8px\" width=\"10\" height=\"20\" > numbers in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/4/e843230b46f5014271411b6dcd70806f20604cde.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_1,b_2,\\cdots,b_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"98\" height=\"16\" > are non-zero.",
    "post_canonical": "Let $\\omega$ be a  $n$ -th primitive root of unity. Given complex numbers $a_1,a_2,\\cdots,a_n$, and $p$ of them are non-zero. Let\n$$b_k=\\sum_{i=1}^n a_i \\omega^{ki}$$\nfor $k=1,2,\\cdots, n$. Prove that if $p>0$, then at least $\\tfrac{n}{p}$ numbers in $b_1,b_2,\\cdots,b_n$ are non-zero.",
